    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "RENTER RESPONSIBILITIES AND RULES",
      "level": 2,
      "style": "SH"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "Renter must have a valid driver's license with motorcycle endorsement (if required by state law for the Vehicle type).",
        "Renter must be at least {{minimum_age}} years old.",
        "Renter must wear a DOT-approved helmet at all times while operating the Vehicle. If Renter does not have their own helmet, Owner-provided helmets must be used.",
        "Renter must wear appropriate protective gear (gloves, eye protection, sturdy footwear, reflective clothing, etc.) as recommended by the manufacturer and applicable laws.",
        "Renter must not operate the Vehicle while intoxicated, under the influence of drugs or alcohol, or otherwise impaired.",
        "Renter is responsible for the Vehicle from the time of pickup until return, including all damage, loss, theft, fines, tickets, and accidents.",
        "Renter must not operate the Vehicle outside of {{allowed_geographic_area}} without Owner's written consent.",
        "Renter must not use the Vehicle for racing, off-road driving (unless equipped and approved for off-road use), stunts, or any illegal or reckless purpose.",
        "Renter must not allow any person not listed on the agreement to operate the Vehicle.",
        "Renter must not carry passengers unless the Vehicle is designed and equipped for passenger carriage and it is legal to do so.",
        "Renter must follow all traffic laws and manufacturer instructions.",
        "Renter must report any accidents, incidents, or mechanical issues to Owner immediately.",
        "{{renter_rules_moto_extra}}"
      ]
    },
